---
/**
 * AB-RR3 · THE HANDOVER
 *
 * A REFINEMENT OF THE LIVE BLOCK, NOT A REPLACEMENT — ab-rr1..rr4, with
 * ab-rr0 carrying the original verbatim so the two can be flipped between on
 * the same harness. Nothing live is touched.
 *
 * WHAT THE ORIGINAL IDEA IS, and all four keep it: a WAVE OF LIGHT travels
 * through type, and BRIGHTNESS IS HANDED from the action to its note. The
 * refusal is the same voice at a smaller scale — ContactForm's own comment
 * says the page should "answer a refusal and an opening in the same voice,
 * at two different scales", and that is the thing worth keeping.
 *
 * WHAT IS WRONG WITH IT IS ALMOST ENTIRELY TIME. Measured from the live CSS:
 *
 *   send-open    520ms a letter on a 26ms stagger  ->  936ms end to end
 *   send-swell   520ms a letter on a 25ms stagger  -> 1070ms end to end
 *   the handover 90ms between the action losing white and the note taking it
 *
 * A WAVE THAT TAKES 936ms TO CROSS SEVENTEEN LETTERS IS A WAVE YOU WAIT FOR,
 * and a refusal that takes 1070ms has finished long after you stopped
 * reading it. Nothing about the idea requires those numbers. Every draft
 * here crosses the action in about 300ms. The refusals differ because two of
 * them buy sequence with time, and all four are measured, not intended:
 * rr1 312ms, rr2 302ms, rr3 423ms, rr4 492ms.
 *
 * ab-se1..se4 replaced the gesture and ab-rf1..rf4 replaced the refusal.
 * These four keep both and sharpen them.

 * ── THIS ONE: THE HANDOVER ──────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * THE ORIGINAL DESCRIBES SOMETHING IT DOES NOT QUITE DO. ContactForm's
 * comment on the refusal reads: "the action gives up its white immediately,
 * the note takes it 90ms later, so the brightness reads as moving from one
 * to the other rather than as two things changing at once." That is exactly
 * the right idea. What is written underneath it is two independent
 * transitions with a 90ms delay on the second — which is two things
 * changing at once, 90ms apart.
 *
 * SO THIS MAKES IT ONE EVENT. The action's letters go dim in sequence from
 * the LEFT, and the note's characters light in the same sequence continuing
 * across the row, so a single quantity of light travels from the far end of
 * "Send this enquiry" to the far end of "Name and email required". The
 * action's seventeen letters run at 7ms, the note's twenty-three pick up
 * where they stop, and the whole crossing takes 423ms — measured: the action
 * dims from 0 to 112ms, the note's first character lights at 119ms, its last
 * starts at 273 and finishes at 423. It is the longest refusal of the four
 * and deliberately so: forty beats of one sequence cannot also be brief.
 *
 * IT IS THE ONE REFINEMENT THAT CHANGES WHAT THE GESTURE MEANS. In the
 * original the two halves both change and you infer a relationship. Here
 * the relationship is the only thing that happens: the note is lit BY the
 * action going out. Nothing is created and nothing is destroyed.
 *
 * THE ROW IS READ LEFT TO RIGHT AND THE LIGHT TRAVELS THAT WAY, which is
 * why the action dims from its left rather than from the end nearest the
 * note. Running it from the right would be shorter but would read as the
 * note pulling light backwards out of the action, which is a different and
 * worse sentence.
 *
 * <- AND THE NOTE'S DELAY IS COMPUTED FROM THE ACTION'S LENGTH. The note
 *   starts at 17 x 7ms = 119ms, so if the action's words are ever rewritten
 *   the handover stays continuous. That is one calc(), and it is the
 *   difference between a relationship and a coincidence.
 */
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const SEND = 'Send this enquiry';
const REFUSE = 'Name and email required';
---

<Base title="The handover — send block draft" description="An isolated draft of the send block's animation.">
  <main class="lab">
      <nav class="sw" aria-label="Variation">
        <span class="sw__t">The handover</span>
        <a class="sw__i" href="/preview/ab-rr0">ORIG</a>
        <a class="sw__i" href="/preview/ab-rr1">RR1</a>
        <a class="sw__i" href="/preview/ab-rr2">RR2</a>
        <a class="sw__i is-here" href="/preview/ab-rr3">RR3</a>
        <a class="sw__i" href="/preview/ab-rr4">RR4</a>
      </nav>

    <div class="lab__head">
      <p class="lab__k">ab-rr3 · The handover</p>
      <p class="lab__d">The handover made literal. Instead of two fades 90ms apart, one quantity of light crosses the row — the action darkens letter by letter from the left as the note lights in the same sweep.</p>
    </div>

    {/* The send block, markup faithful to ContactForm.astro: the sentence is
        written once for assistive tech and once as letters, and the letters
        are hidden from it. */}
    <div class="send" data-send>
      <div class="send__band">
        <a class="send__act" id="send" href="#" aria-disabled="true">
          <span class="visually-hidden">{SEND}</span>
          <span class="send__chars" aria-hidden="true">{SEND.split('').map((c, i) => (
            <i style={`--i:${i}`}>{c === ' ' ? '\u00A0' : c}</i>
          ))}</span>
          <span class="send__arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
        <p class="mono send__note" id="note"></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="lab__ctl">
      <button type="button" data-act="wake">Wake the action</button>
      <button type="button" data-act="refuse">Refuse</button>
      <button type="button" data-act="ready">Ready note</button>
      <button type="button" data-act="reset">Reset</button>
      <span class="lab__state" data-state></span>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>

<script is:inline define:vars={{ REFUSE }}>
  (function () {
    const shell = document.querySelector('[data-send]');
    const act = document.getElementById('send');
    const note = document.getElementById('note');
    const state = document.querySelector('[data-state]');
    const READY = 'Opens as a draft. Send it when you\u2019re ready.';

    /* ASTRO SCOPES THIS PAGE'S CSS BY STAMPING data-astro-cid-* ON EVERY
       ELEMENT IN THE TEMPLATE, and compiling `.send__ink` to
       `.send__ink[data-astro-cid-…]`. The note's characters are built here,
       so they are not in the template and never get stamped — and every
       rule below that targets .send__ink or .send__ink i would silently
       fail to match. Measured before this was added: the refusal ran its
       animation on nothing and the note stayed --dim.

       ContactForm.astro solves it the same way. Copying the attribute off
       the note itself keeps the stylesheet ordinary: no :global, no inline
       styles. (HANDOFF §6.) */
    const scope = Array.from(note.attributes).map((a) => a.name)
      .find((n) => n.startsWith('data-astro-cid-'));
    const stamp = (el) => { if (scope) el.setAttribute(scope, ''); return el; };

    /* The same split ContactForm's setNote() uses: one span for a screen
       reader, one per character for the ink. */
    function setNote(text) {
      note.textContent = '';
      const said = stamp(document.createElement('span'));
      said.className = 'visually-hidden';
      said.textContent = text;
      const ink = stamp(document.createElement('span'));
      ink.className = 'send__ink';
      ink.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
      for (let i = 0; i < text.length; i++) {
        const ch = stamp(document.createElement('i'));
        ch.style.setProperty('--i', String(i));
        ch.textContent = text[i];
        ink.appendChild(ch);
      }
      note.append(said, ink);
    }

    function say(s) { state.textContent = s; }

    function reset() {
      act.classList.remove('is-ready', 'is-woken');
      shell.classList.remove('is-asking');
      act.setAttribute('aria-disabled', 'true');
      setNote(REFUSE);
      say('idle — not ready');
    }

    /* Re-adding a class does not restart an animation unless the element is
       reflowed in between. */
    function restart(el, cls) {
      el.classList.remove(cls);
      void el.offsetWidth;
      el.classList.add(cls);
    }

    document.querySelector('.lab__ctl').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
      const b = e.target.closest('[data-act]');
      if (!b) return;
      const a = b.dataset.act;
      if (a === 'reset') return reset();
      if (a === 'wake') {
        act.classList.add('is-ready');
        act.setAttribute('aria-disabled', 'false');
        shell.classList.remove('is-asking');
        setNote(READY);
        restart(act, 'is-woken');
        say('woken — ready');
      }
      if (a === 'refuse') {
        act.classList.remove('is-ready', 'is-woken');
        act.setAttribute('aria-disabled', 'true');
        setNote(REFUSE);
        restart(shell, 'is-asking');
        say('refused');
      }
      if (a === 'ready') { setNote(READY); say('ready note'); }
    });

    act.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      if (!act.classList.contains('is-ready')) {
        setNote(REFUSE);
        restart(shell, 'is-asking');
        say('refused');
      }
    });

    reset();
  })();
</script>

<style>
  /* ══ THE HARNESS ═════════════════════════════════════════════════
     Not design. Enough page to judge the block on, and controls to replay
     the states without filling a form at the bottom of a 15,000px page. */
  .lab {
    min-height: 100vh; padding: clamp(28px, 7vh, 80px) var(--margin);
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; gap: 44px;
    max-width: 980px;
  }
  .lab__k {
    margin: 0 0 8px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: var(--t-micro);
    letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent);
  }
  .lab__d { margin: 0; max-width: 62ch; color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--t-sm); line-height: 1.5; }
  .lab__ctl { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; align-items: center; }
  .lab__ctl button {
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted);
    background: transparent; border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding: 9px 14px; border-radius: 999px; cursor: pointer;
    transition: color 140ms linear, border-color 140ms linear;
  }
  .lab__ctl button:hover { color: var(--bone); border-color: var(--bone-dim); }
  .lab__state {
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--dim); margin-left: 6px;
  }
  .sw {
    position: fixed; top: 14px; right: 16px; z-index: 40;
    display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px;
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: var(--t-micro);
    letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .sw__t { color: var(--muted); }
  .sw a { color: var(--dim); text-decoration: none; transition: color 140ms linear; }
  .sw a:hover { color: var(--bone); }
  .sw a.is-here { color: var(--accent); }
  .sw a.sw__i--src { color: var(--muted); margin-left: 5px; }

  /* ══ THE BLOCK, AS THE SITE HAS IT ═══════════════════════════════
     Structure and type copied from ContactForm.astro so the draft is judged
     at the real size and in the real layout. Everything the VARIATION
     changes is in the block below this one. */
  .send__band {
    display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: var(--s-2); flex-wrap: wrap;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-top: 26px;
  }
  .send__act {
    font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.06vw, 2.75rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.035em; line-height: 1;
    color: var(--bone); text-decoration: none; white-space: nowrap;
    display: inline-flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.3em;
    cursor: not-allowed;
  }
  .send__act.is-ready { cursor: pointer; }
  .send__chars i, .send__ink i { display: inline-block; font-style: normal; }
  .send__arrow { display: inline-block; }
  .send__note {
    margin: 0 0 0 auto; text-align: right;
    color: var(--dim); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.8; max-width: 32ch;
  }
  .send__ink { display: inline-block; white-space: pre-wrap; transform-origin: right center; }
  @media (max-width: 620px) {
    .send__band { flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; }
    .send__note { margin-left: 0; text-align: left; }
    .send__ink { transform-origin: left center; }
    .send__act { white-space: normal; }
  }

  /* ══ RR3 · THE HANDOVER ══════════════════════════════════════════
     One quantity of light crosses the row: the action goes out from the
     left and the note lights in the same sequence, continuing. */
  .send__act.is-woken .send__chars i {
    animation: send-open 190ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.9, 0.2, 1);
    animation-delay: calc(var(--i) * 7ms);
  }
  @keyframes send-open {
    from { color: var(--dim); transform: translateY(0.06em); }
    to   { color: inherit; transform: none; }
  }
  .send__arrow { transition: transform 140ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.9, 0.2, 1); }
  .send__act.is-ready:hover { color: var(--accent); }
  .send__act.is-ready:hover .send__arrow { transform: translateX(0.28em); }

  /* The action goes out, letter by letter, from the left. */
  .send.is-asking .send__act { transform: translateX(-4px); }
  .send.is-asking .send__chars i {
    animation: rr3-give 150ms linear both;
    animation-delay: calc(var(--i) * 7ms);
  }
  @keyframes rr3-give { to { color: var(--dim); } }
  .send.is-asking .send__arrow {
    animation: rr3-give 150ms linear both;
    animation-delay: 119ms;
  }

  /* The note takes it, continuing the same sequence. 17 letters x 7ms is
     where the action's own run ends — computed, not typed, so the two stay
     joined if the words are ever rewritten. */
  .send__ink { transform-origin: right center; }
  .send.is-asking .send__ink {
    transform: scale(1.08);
    transition: transform 170ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.9, 0.2, 1) calc(17 * 7ms);
  }
  .send.is-asking .send__ink i {
    animation: rr3-take 150ms linear both;
    animation-delay: calc(17 * 7ms + var(--i) * 7ms);
  }
  @keyframes rr3-take {
    from { color: var(--dim); }
    to   { color: var(--bone); }
  }
</style>
